ctations that the US Federal Reserve has concluded its monetary tightening cycle. Emerging signals from the central bank indicated that interest rates have reached their peak, which eased concerns over rising borrowing costs and strengthened investor sentiment.\nRecent inflation data also played a supporting role, as core inflation readings came in lower than anticipated. This reduced the probability of further interest rate hikes, improving investment sentiment and prompting traders to increase their allocation to higher-risk assets, particularly equities.\nThe technology sector was identified as the main engine of the rally. Qasimia pointed out that Nvidia continues to lead, benefiting from robust demand for artificial intelligence chips and data centers. A global surge in AI-related investment has boosted the company's expected revenues and profits, positively affecting its share price and market capitalization.\nQasimia emphasized that technology sector gains were not solely based on expectations but were backed by strong financial results from the first quarter of 2026. Reports indicated that approximately 80 percent of listed companies reported earnings that surpassed analyst estimates, marking one of the highest rates of such outperformance since the second quarter of 2021. These results exceeded expectations by significant margins, reinforcing confidence in the solid financial and economic underpinnings of the current rally.\nAnother supportive factor was the decline in US Treasury bond yields for ten-year maturities, which fell below 4.6 percent and approached the 4.5 percent level. Lower yields typically enhance the attractiveness of equities relative to fixed-income instruments, encouraging investors to redirect funds toward stock markets for higher returns.\nA drop in oil prices during the recent period also helped reduce pressure on corporate profit margins and lowered operating and production costs, positively influencing future earnings expectations across many sectors.\nQasimia highlighted a notable return of retail investors, fueled by improved market sentiment and rising confidence. Observers suggest that regulatory simplifications and developments concerning individual investment accounts may encourage additional liquidity inflows into markets in the coming months, boosting activity and trading volumes.\nMassive spending on artificial intelligence remains the primary driver of US market gains. Estimates indicate that capital investments related to AI have increased by approximately USD 130 billion recently, amid a global race among major companies to build AI infrastructure and expand technological capabilities.\nGeopolitical developments also influenced market movements. Signals of de-escalation in several international issues helped reduce the uncertainty that had been weighing on investors, positively affecting risk appetite and sustaining fund flows into equity markets.\nThe gains achieved by US markets in May appear driven by a combination of monetary and economic factors, strong corporate results, and the ongoing surge in the AI sector. While challenges persist, current data suggests investors are betting on continued growth and an improving business environment, explaining why US indices have reached new record levels, Qasimia concluded.\nIn this Article\n^GSPC 0.84% ^TNX -0.64% CL=F 0.64% ^DJI 0.02% ^IXIC 1.71% NVDA 1.75%\nS\u0026P 500\n\n--------\n搜索关键词：2026年5月31日 美股收盘 纳斯达克 道琼斯 标普500\n\n网页标题：6月1日财经早餐:特朗普收紧伊核意向协议条款，金价坚守4540上方，美油触及90关口_新浪财经\n\n网页链接：http://m.toutiao.com/group/7646206166896247337/\n\n发布时间：2026-06-01T07:45:20+08:00\n\n网页内容：来源:滚动播报\n汇通财经APP讯——周一(北京时间6月1日)亚市早盘，现货黄金交投于4542美元/盎司附近，美联储年内加息概率略有下降，约为48.2%，支撑金价，同时特朗普收紧伊核意向协议条款，同时，据悉伊朗将按自身立场修订伊美协议草案，伊朗议会议长表示，在确认伊朗人民权利得到保障前，不会批准任何协议，受此影响，油价回升，美原油开盘上涨近3%，触及90美元/桶关口上方，现交投于89.51美元/桶附近。\n股市\n美股上周五收盘创下历史新高，三大股指周线和月线均收涨，受科技股走强及中东协议前景提振，标普500指数上涨0.21%收于7579.74点，纳斯达克综合指数上涨0.20%收于26971.21点，道琼斯工业平均指数上涨0.72%收于51032.45点。\n戴尔上调全年业绩预期后股价大涨，带动科技板块走高，市场对人工智能的乐观情绪